   "properties": {},
   "widgets_values": [
    "## unirig-humanoid-workflow.json\n\nUniRig (Linux only)\n\n**Does:** auto-rigs a humanoid mesh and exports a **Mixamo-compatible FBX** (Unity-friendly).\n**View:** `UniRigPreviewRiggedMesh` shows the rigged FBX with its skeleton in the canvas; the path is also written to text by `SaveText`.\n**Platform:** **Linux only** \u2014 UniRig needs `bpy` (Blender-as-Python), which the pack provides\nin its own pixi/conda env. It failed on Windows with a native DLL error (E4).\n**See:** `3d/EXPERIMENTS.md` E4-L, `3d/pipeline-design.md`.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S12** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E4-L** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   ],
   "widgets_values_named": {
    "text": "## unirig-humanoid-workflow.json\n\nUniRig (Linux only)\n\n**Does:** auto-rigs a humanoid mesh and exports a **Mixamo-compatible FBX** (Unity-friendly).\n**View:** `UniRigPreviewRiggedMesh` shows the rigged FBX with its skeleton in the canvas; the path is also written to text by `SaveText`.\n**Platform:** **Linux only** \u2014 UniRig needs `bpy` (Blender-as-Python), which the pack provides\nin its own pixi/conda env. It failed on Windows with a native DLL error (E4).\n**See:** `3d/EXPERIMENTS.md` E4-L, `3d/pipeline-design.md`.\n\n---\n*How to run it: story **S12** in `HOWTO.md`  \u00b7  Why it is this way: **E4-L** in the scenarios' `EXPERIMENTS` logs.*"
   },
